<title>INDIA: POLL-Tata Power 6-mth net seen lower.</title>
<headline>POLL-Tata Power 6-mth net seen lower.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's Tata Power Company Ltd's net profit is projected to drop 11.4 percent to 760.22 million rupees in the first half of fiscal 1997/98 (April-March), a poll consensus showed on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Sales in the first six months to September 30, 1997 are forecast to decline 5.2 percent to 6.5 billion rupees from 6.9 billion rupees in the year-ago period, 18 leading brokerages and securities firms said.</p>
<p>Following are the details of the poll compared with actuals for the first half of 1996/97.</p>
<p>------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>				NET PROFIT		   SALES</p>
<p>				   (first half to September 30)</p>
<p>			    97/98     96/97	97/98	96/97</p>
<p>					 (in millions of rupees)</p>
<p>-------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>TATA POWER  ----PAT seen down 11.4%, sales 5.2%</p>
<p>Average		  760.22    858.60     6,544.58   6,907.40</p>
<p>High		   1,200.00		  11,600.00</p>
<p>Low			410.00		   5,575.00</p>
<p>--Bombay newsroom +91-22-265-9000</p>
